From f10d87ef9c63bbcbeb150964a80084e06352b085 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Liora Guo <liora.guo.wiwynn@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 6 Nov 2025 07:34:47 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] yosemite4: fb-ipmi-oem: skip FRU read when motherboard
 path is missing

[Task Description]
On YosemiteV4 platforms, when the motherboard FRU path cannot be resolved, getFruData() now returns -1 instead of falling back to a
generic selection. This prevents showing SN/PN from the wrong FRU.

[Root Cause]
- Related to YV4T1M-480
- During AC-off, Entity-Manager prunes inventory objects, so getMotherBoardFruPath() can be empty. The previous fallback tried to
  reconstruct a path by matching "_<pos>", which is unsafe on YV4 because non-motherboard objects can also match (e.g. "BRCM_OCP_NIC_FRU_1").
  This could silently report FRU data for the wrong object. Failing fast avoids misinformation.

[Solution]
- In getFruData(), when getMotherBoardFruPath() returns empty, replace:
    else { baseBoard = "Baseboard"; }
  with:
    else { return -1; }
- No interface or parameter changes. Behavior only changes for the
  path-missing case.

[Test Plan]
- Verified on debug card: FRU info renders correctly.
- Conditional display: Show motherboard FRU SN/PN only if getMotherBoardFruPath() exists; otherwise display "Not Found".
---
 src/oemcommands.cpp | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/oemcommands.cpp b/src/oemcommands.cpp
index 0f8d0e8..958e9ec 100644
--- a/src/oemcommands.cpp
+++ b/src/oemcommands.cpp
@@ -704,7 +704,7 @@ int8_t getFruData(std::string& data, std::string& name)
     }
     else
     {
-        baseBoard = "Baseboard";
+        return -1;
     }
 
     bool platform = isMultiHostPlatform();
